      "writtenOn": "2014-03-06T01:06:55Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "So you are saying that your new code will do the blocking on case of SystemReady? If true then, there is a scenario  1. On SystemReady - you might block \n2. Next, the API ActivityManagerService.switchUser might block because (oldUserId \u003d\u003d userId).\n\nThe result will be that nothing was done.\n\nAn other thing is that - I don\u0027t think it is ok to solve HW problems on framework layer, because there are many HW types each has its own \"walk around\"s needs.",
      "parentUuid": "1c7df19f_cd4104c7",
